@inject Profiler.Web.Data.SnapshotOptions Snapshots
@{
    ViewBag.Title = "Privacy";
}

<div class="page-wrap">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="page-header">
            <h1>🔒 How Profiler Protects Your Data</h1>
            <p>Privacy is not a setting here — it is the architecture.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3 class="mb-2">What we store</h3>
                <p>
                    When you connect a source or pick interests, we extract short interest labels (like
                    <code>language:python</code> or <code>genre:sci-fi</code>) and immediately run them
                    through a <strong>MinHash</strong> algorithm. Only the resulting numeric signature is
                    kept. Everything else the database holds is listed below — the list is generated from
                    the database schema itself, so it cannot fall behind the product. Your own copy of all
                    of it is on your <a href="/account/data">data page</a>.
                </p>
                <div style="overflow-x:auto">
                    <table class="data-table">
                        <thead>
                            <tr><th>What</th><th>Exactly what is kept</th><th>Your control</th></tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            @foreach (var kind in Profiler.Web.Data.DataInventory.Kinds)
                            {
                                <tr>
                                    <th scope="row">@kind.Name</th>
                                    <td>@kind.What</td>
                                    <td>@kind.Control</td>
                                </tr>
                            }
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3 class="mb-2">What we never store</h3>
                <ul style="padding-left:1.25rem">
                    <li>Raw interest data — book titles, watch history, starred repos, playlists, channel names, or the interests you ticked or typed</li>
                    <li>Access tokens and API keys — used once to fetch your data and discarded</li>
                    <li>Uploaded CSV files — parsed in memory, never written to disk</li>
                    <li>Your answers to the values questionnaire — only the derived bucket is kept</li>
                    <li>An email address or phone number — none is asked for. A contact line exists only if you type one, and only you decide what it says</li>
                    <li>Who invited whom to a circle, or the invite links you shared</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3 class="mb-2">Why matching still works</h3>
                <p>
                    Two MinHash signatures can be compared to estimate how similar the underlying
                    interest sets are (Jaccard similarity) without either side revealing what those
                    interests are. Other people only ever see your username, a match tier and an
                    approximate percentage, which source types you have in common, the circles you both
                    are in, and whatever you chose to make public — and all of that only while you are
                    discoverable.
                </p>
                <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                    A signature is not reversible on its own, and it is additionally hashed with a
                    secret held by this server and never stored beside it — so a copy of the database
                    alone cannot be tested against a list of guessed interests to see which ones
                    were yours.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3 class="mb-2">You stay in control</h3>
                <p>
                    Disconnect any source from your dashboard at any time — its signature is
                    deleted immediately and your fingerprint is rebuilt without it. You can also
                    delete your entire account from the dashboard, which permanently removes your
                    user record, fingerprint, and every per-source signature.
                </p>
                @if (Snapshots.Enabled)
                {
                    <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                        For disaster recovery this server keeps rolling snapshots of its database; any snapshot
                        older than <strong>@Snapshots.RetentionDays days</strong> is deleted on the server's next daily pass. They hold the same
                        signatures as the live database — never raw data — stay on the same server, and anything
                        you delete is gone from them by then.
                    </p>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
